=== TAKE 10 / TAKE 20 RULES ===

Take 10: Eligible when the character can act carefully — no combat, no imminent threats,
no rushing. Treats the d20 as 10. INELIGIBLE when: active combat, immediate danger,
fleeing, chasing, or any situation where the character cannot pause to be methodical.

Take 20: Eligible when ALL of:
  (a) Take 10 is eligible,
  (b) failure has no consequences (no trap trigger, no alarm, no damage), AND
  (c) the character can physically stop and retry ~20 times over ~40 minutes.
INELIGIBLE when ANY of these apply:
  - Take 10 is ineligible
  - Failure has consequences (trap, alarm, damage, alert enemies)
  - The character is running, chasing, fleeing, or pursuing a moving target
  - A concrete deadline exists (flooding room, closing gate, ritual timer, target escaping)
  - The action is inherently one-shot (jumping a gap, catching a falling object)

Both apply ONLY to skill checks, never attack rolls, saving throws, or ability checks.
When context is sparse and nothing indicates danger, pressure, or consequences, default
to eligible. Do NOT deny based on absence of information alone.

=== INSTRUCTIONS ===

Evaluate the player's action across all six domains (traversal, combat, social,
exploration, rest, inventory) in a single pass. For each domain:

1. BEACON: Determine if the action affects this domain. Set "affected" to true ONLY if
   the action DIRECTLY and IMMEDIATELY changes that domain's game state. Most actions
   affect only 1-2 domains — be conservative.

2. MECHANICS (only if affected AND needs_mechanics is true): Determine what player rolls,
   NPC actions, and automatic consequences are required in this domain.
   IMPORTANT: Only request rolls the rules actually require. Many actions simply succeed:
   - Casting a prepared spell in safe conditions requires NO roll.
   - Walking, riding a trained mount on a road, or routine movement requires NO roll.
   - Using an item or equipping gear requires NO roll unless rules say otherwise.
   If no rolls are needed, return EMPTY player_rolls for that domain.
   Every roll MUST include a numeric "dc" value.

3. ROLL QUALIFICATION (only for skill checks): For each roll, assess whether Take 10 and
   Take 20 are eligible based on the situational context across ALL domains. Also note
   any situational modifiers (flanking, cover, environmental conditions, etc.).

4. Set macro_significant to true ONLY for major story beats (completing a quest, defeating
   a boss, discovering a critical secret). False for routine actions.

5. Do NOT request duplicate rolls. If a skill check (e.g., Perception DC 10) is needed
   for multiple domains, include it in ONE domain only — the most relevant one.

